Allocated leaf return signing — 2026-10-16

pac-ret omits signing only for an allocated frameless leaf whose x30 never
leaves its register. Every stored x30 is signed. pac-ret+leaf also signs the
frameless leaf. Only -mno-omit-leaf-frame-pointer forces an unnecessary leaf
record. Calls, spills, fixed storage, dynamic allocation, activation reads,
incoming stack arguments, variadic areas, canaries and opaque assembly keep
the record. Other optional selection/allocation/frame protection is unchanged.
CFI tracks the actual frame and signing state. Option order also controls the
ACLE macro through the same effective policy.

Three policy tests cover both targets at O0/O2, both PAC scopes and both leaf
requests. Lowering-inserted 128-bit helper calls and patchable NOP entries are
included. The existing sealed Linux unwind/canary test passes all eight
unsigned/signed and frame-variant combinations.

Sixteen native executions pass: both scopes, leaf requests and O0/O2 on
Darwin's normal ABI and Linux with -mgeneral-regs-only. The unchanged runtime
fixture includes nested calls, multiple returns, nine arguments, varargs,
dynamic storage and activation addresses. Four Linux source-path checks pass.
Four Darwin source checks fail at va_start (the memory model assumes a 32-byte
list). A separate Darwin general-only compilation refuses synthetic SIMD
fillers for the ninth named integer argument. Neither refusal is a PASS or silently discarded input.
The retained record separates these pre-existing boundaries from PAC behavior.

Original hot units compile and assemble; nothing is installed or booted:
Unit                        Saved x30 before/after   Object bytes before/after
mm/page_alloc.o                          168 / 149            527664 / 527104
arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.o                       89 / 74            703416 / 703048
crypto/sha3_generic.o                       6 / 6             253720 / 253720
Each saved-x30 count equals its paciasp count. Object bytes are not .text.
The same 41 disclosed probe omissions remain, zero unreviewed omissions.

Capture: .evidence/return-signing-20261016/ (500 MiB cap).
baseline.json preserves the old leaf behavior. runtime.json records every
command, source and binary; both failed attempts remain separately. Probe
records are kernel-probes.signing.json and kernel-assembly.signing.json under
.evidence/live-range-holes-20261016/. Their six hashed .s/.o intermediates
total 11415685 bytes and are retired after a no-open-handle check. Exact
intermediate probe files are no longer retained; current runtimes remain.
All eight Linux runtime programs also exit zero in one TCG run with the
retained GCC kernel and neoverse-n2 CPU; input hashes stay unchanged. This is
execution coverage, not a new-kernel boot or tracing result.
The unchanged array reduction is now 195 instructions/call and 824 function
bytes (200/844 before signing admission); the record remains 61/312. The
helper reduction is 32/152 (37/172 before). All three container and three TCG
runs exit zero with their prior checksums, zero dropped/irregular blocks and
disjoint executable addresses. Both N09/N10 2x thresholds remain unmet.
Combined acceptance: 454 Rust suites, 3449 passed, zero failed, eight ignored;
Clippy and formatting pass. All six Lean steps pass. These gates do not
extend the checked proof subset to Darwin or return authentication.
Private-storage/signing captures use 84300 KiB together. The existing target
cache grows 336432 KiB from the 09:12 baseline; probe captures add 96 KiB net.
The helper capture shrinks 60 KiB. Combined measured growth is 420768 KiB;
shared-cache growth is not attributed to signing alone. Free space: 50 GiB.
Kernel stack traces, ftrace and kprobes remain separate acceptance obligations.
